 "name": "armoured quadruped (Cragjaw ground drake)",
 "comment": "Bone head/tail in the rigger frame: Blender Z-up after its 180-degree Z turn, +Y forward (snout), left = -X. reference_bounds is the Cragjaw mesh bbox measured in that frame, so the fit is identity for this mesh. No wing* bones (the membrane field and the wing bind correction skip themselves). Four splayed legs: hind on thigh/shin/ankle/foot/toe_hind, front on upper_arm/forearm/wrist/hand/toe_fore, four toes each as the mesh has. Long heavy tail, eight segments, drooping from z 0.33 at the rump to 0.16 at the tip; the spine sits at z ~0.34 (belly 0.12, plate ridge 0.55). The skull is the anvil from y 0.29 to the snout at 0.487; the jaw bone runs through the middle of the mandible from the hinge at (0.33, 0.275) to (0.465, 0.235); the mouth line is at z ~0.30 and the jutting mandible below it.",
